+
+
+### Portable local transcript export
+
+`ai://agendrain.json` is a generated, read-only file: copy it with F5 to
+export the current dialog in agendrain version 1 JSON. Copy `ctx/` alongside
+it only when an importer will explicitly be allowed to include file contents;
+references in the JSON use paths such as `ctx/example.go`. The export itself
+contains no context file contents, image bytes, API keys or GitHub tokens.
+It is generated outside the bounded context tree and is never included in
+VTPACK requests.
+
+Each `Session.ask` attempt records its base instructions, patch-mode prompt,
+other generated instructions, model, context file references, history
+compaction level and outcome at request time. Those records are saved in the
+existing dialog JSON under the optional `requests` field, so an archive or
+restart preserves earlier instructions, including failed attempts and the
+names of files removed later. Raw provider error messages are not exported.
+Dialogs saved before recording began retain their turns and current file
+references; a warning explains that their historical instructions are missing.
+Current settings are never presented as evidence of historical instructions.
+
+This export covers the Session dialog. Standalone bot, manager, worker and
+`RunAgent` tool histories have no persistent Session ownership; only reports
+actually added to the dialog are available here. A separate capture mechanism
+is needed before those transient conversations can be exported in full.
